course: dictionary
lesson: 1352
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around a word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Children having cancer treatment must avoid germs, because the treatment makes it harder to fight infections.» Treatment and infections are about the body, so cancer here is an illness.
explain: Look for a capital letter too. A capital C can change a word completely. «The equator, the Tropic of Cancer, the Tropic of Capricorn and the Arctic Circle are lines of latitude.» Here Cancer is a name on a map, not an illness.
explain: Ask: what meaning fits here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. If it does not, try the other meaning.
fact: Cancer is a serious illness in which some cells in the body grow out of control and can spread.
fact: A cancer is one kind of this illness, such as «skin cancer».
fact: With a capital C, Cancer is a group of stars and a star sign.
fact: Most illnesses get better, and many serious ones, even many cancers, can be treated.
fact: You cannot catch cancer from someone, and illness is never a child's fault.
exercise: «Children having cancer treatment must avoid germs.» What does cancer mean here? | A kind of sun cream | A group of stars in the night sky | A line on a map | *An illness
exercise: «The Tropic of Cancer is a line of latitude on the map.» What is Cancer in this sentence? | A cell that grows too fast | A kind of skin | A serious illness in the body | *A line on a map
exercise: «Wear sun cream to protect your skin from skin cancer.» What kind of cancer is meant? | *Skin cancer | Lung cancer | Cancer of the stars | The Tropic of Cancer
test: What is cancer, in its first meaning? | *A serious illness in which some cells grow out of control | A group of stars with a capital C | A line of latitude on a map | A kind of sun cream
test: «Cancer» with a capital C in «Leo was born under Cancer» means what? | A type of skin | *A star sign and a group of stars | A serious illness | A petrol station
exam: How can you tell which meaning of cancer a writer wants? | Pick the first meaning you remember | *Read the context and check your meaning still makes sense in the sentence | Skip the word and never come back to it | Look only at whether there is a capital letter
